      "text": "First, we need to identify the total number of possible meals that Crystal can buy. To do this, we count the number of options available for each category and then multiply them together.\n\nFor the entrees, there are 4 options (Pizza, Chicken Teriyaki, Corn Dog, and Fish and Chips). \n\nFor the drinks, there are 2 options (Lemonade and Root Beer).\n\nFor the desserts, there are 2 options (Frozen Yogurt and Chocolate Chip Cookie).\n\nSince Crystal can choose one entree, one drink, and one dessert, we multiply the number of options in each category together:\n\nTotal number of distinct possible meals = (number of entrees) × (number of drinks) × (number of desserts)\n= 4 × 2 × 2\n= 16\n\nTherefore, Crystal can buy 16 distinct possible meals from the options available in the food court.",
