      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the total number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy, we need to consider the choices available for each category: entrees, drinks, and desserts. We will use the fundamental principle of counting, which states that if there are \\( n \\) ways to do one thing and \\( m \\) ways to do another, then there are \\( n \\times m \\) ways to do both.\n\nFirst, let's count the number of choices for each category:\n- There are 4 entrees: Pizza, Chicken Teriyaki, Corn Dog, Fish and Chips.\n- There are 2 drinks: Lemonade, Root Beer.\n- There are 2 desserts: Frozen Yogurt, Chocolate Chip Cookie.\n\nNow, we will calculate the total number of distinct possible meals by multiplying the number of choices for each category:\n\\[\n4 \\text{ (entrees)} \\times 2 \\text{ (drinks)} \\times 2 \\text{ (desserts)} = 4 \\times 2 \\times 2 = 16\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy is \\(\\boxed{16}\\).",
