      "sample_index": 4,
      "text": "To determine the number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy, we need to consider all combinations of entrees, drinks, and desserts. Let's break it down step by step:\n\n1. **Identify the options for each category:**\n   - Entrees: Pizza, Chicken Teriyaki, Corn Dog, Fish and Chips\n   - Drinks: Lemonade, Root Beer\n   - Desserts: Frozen Yogurt, Chocolate Chip Cookie\n\n2. **Calculate the total number of combinations:**\n   - For each entree, Crystal can choose any of the 4 drinks.\n   - For each entree, she can also choose any of the 2 desserts.\n\n3. **Multiply the number of choices for each category:**\n   - There are 4 entrees and 2 desserts, so the total number of combinations is:\n     \\[\n     4 \\text{ (entrees)} \\times 2 \\text{ (desserts)} = 8 \\text{ (combinations per entree)}\n     \\]\n   - Since there are 4 entrees, the total number of distinct possible meals is:\n     \\[\n     4 \\text{ (entrees)} \\times 8 \\text{ (combinations per entree)} = 32 \\text{ (total combinations)}\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy is \\(\\boxed{32}\\).",
